This notice does not cover the underlying public data, which remains the
work of its publishers and carries its own terms:

  NH GRANIT (University of New Hampshire) — water bodies, streams,
    conservation land, town and state boundaries, public water access sites
  NH Fish and Game — waterfowl zone descriptions, seasons, bag limits,
    closed-area rules
  MassGIS (Commonwealth of Massachusetts) — 1:25,000 hydrography, Office of
    Fishing and Boating Access sites, Protected and Recreational OpenSpace,
    municipalities
  MassWildlife — waterfowl zone descriptions, seasons, bag limits
  Maine Department of Inland Fisheries and Wildlife — waterfowl zone
    descriptions and Coastal Zone polygon, seasons, bag limits, closed areas,
    wildlife management areas
  Maine GeoLibrary, Maine Coastal Program, Maine Conserved Lands, Maine E911
    road centerlines and town boundaries (State of Maine)
  Rhode Island Department of Environmental Management — seasons, bag limits,
    the late-season goose area, restricted waterfowl areas, state hunting
    land, special hunting areas, fishing and boating access
  Rhode Island Coastal Resources Management Council — public shoreline
    rights-of-way
  RIGIS (Rhode Island Geographic Information System) — municipal boundaries
  U.S. Census Bureau TIGER — local road centerlines (one connector on the
    Rhode Island late-goose line)
  U.S. Geological Survey — National Hydrography Dataset (lakes, marshes,
    wide rivers and bays, streams)
  U.S. Fish and Wildlife Service National Wetlands Inventory — marsh, for
    the habitat surface
  U.S. Fish and Wildlife Service — National Hunt Units, Great Bay NWR
  U.S. Census Bureau TIGER — state outlines
  NOAA CO-OPS — tide predictions
  OpenStreetMap contributors — road geometry, under the Open Database
    License (openstreetmap.org/copyright)

Nothing here is legal advice and nothing here is an official source. Season
dates, bag limits and closed areas change. Check the state agency before
you hunt.
